# [M6.4.3] D27 blinded corpus -- atomic-groups module.
#
# The --features refusal direction, both ways, for otherwise-VALID PCRE2
# syntax (contrast with syntax_errors.rxt, which is genuinely malformed
# syntax with the module ENABLED). This file is pcrec-CLI-level, not a
# PCRE2 semantics claim -- MOD-0.3c's own module-gate mechanism -- so it
# was measured directly against `build/pcrec`'s CLI (not the libpcre2
# oracle, which has no such gate and always has every construct "on").
#
# Two blocks per pattern:
#   1. no `features` line at all -- the module is DISABLED (pcrec's
#      default feature set is "std1" = {classes, modifiers}, and
#      atomic-groups is not in it) -- pcrec must refuse.
#   2. `features atomic-groups` -- the module is ENABLED, but (measured
#      directly against the CLI on this cell's prebuilt, pre-
#      implementation `build/pcrec`) still not implemented -- pcrec must
#      still refuse, for a DIFFERENT reason.
# docs/testing.md's perr rule asserts only the exit code (nonzero), never
# the message text, so both blocks pass identically today; what this file
# pins down is that BOTH directions are refused, not just one.
#
# A finding worth a look at merge review, not a change this corpus makes:
# measured directly, `(?>...)` DOES distinguish the two refusal reasons
# in its message text ("requires module" vs "is enabled but ... is not
# implemented yet"), but every possessive-quantifier spelling tested here
# (`a++`, `a*+`, `a?+`, `a{2,3}+`, `a{,3}+`, `a{2,}+`) gives the IDENTICAL
# "possessive quantifier requires module 'atomic-groups'" message in BOTH
# directions -- the possessive-quantifier parse path does not appear to
# consult whether the module is enabled before emitting that message,
# unlike the `(?>...)` path. Not asserted here (perr is exit-code-only,
# and message wording is explicitly not pcrec's promise per CLAUDE.md's
# Compatibility Standard D26), but worth an implementer's attention since
# it suggests the two constructs' gating checks are not sharing one code
# path today.

# --- (?>...) ---

pattern (?>ab)
perr

pattern (?>ab)
features atomic-groups
perr

# --- a++ ---

pattern a++
perr

pattern a++
features atomic-groups
perr

# --- a*+ ---

pattern a*+
perr

pattern a*+
features atomic-groups
perr

# --- a?+ ---

pattern a?+
perr

pattern a?+
features atomic-groups
perr

# --- a{2,3}+ (bounded brace-possessive) ---

pattern a{2,3}+
perr

pattern a{2,3}+
features atomic-groups
perr

# --- a{,3}+ (PCRE2 10.43+ {,n} spelling, possessive) ---

pattern a{,3}+
perr

pattern a{,3}+
features atomic-groups
perr

# --- a{2,}+ (unbounded brace-possessive) ---

pattern a{2,}+
perr

pattern a{2,}+
features atomic-groups
perr
